lse,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.004184619176268889,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":44.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.029209958831601646,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":51.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.87289,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bausch + Lomb Corporation operates as an eye health company in the United States, Puerto Rico, China, France, Japan, Germany, the United Kingdom, Canada, Russia, Spain, Italy, Mexico, Poland, and internationally. It operates in three segments: Vision Care, Pharmaceuticals, and Surgical. The Vision Care segment provides contact lens that covers the spectrum of wearing modalities, including daily disposable and frequently replaced contact lenses; and contact lenses that are indicated for therapeutic use and provide optical correction during healing. It also offers contact lens care products, eye vitamins, mineral supplements, and over-the-counter eye drops that address various conditions, such as eye allergies, conjunctivitis, dry eye, and redness relief. The Pharmaceuticals segment offers proprietary and generic pharmaceutical products for post-operative treatments, as well as for the treatment of glaucoma, eye inflammation, ocular hypertension, dry eyes, and retinal diseases. The Surgical segment provides medical device equipment, consumables, and technologies for the treatment of cataracts, corneal, vitreous, and retinal eye conditions; and intraocular lenses and delivery systems, phacoemulsification equipment, and other surgical instruments and devices for cataract surgery. The company sells its products and services through direct sales forces and independent distributors. Bausch + Lomb Corporation was founded in 1853 and is headquartered in Vaughan, Canada. Bausch + Lomb Corporation operates as a subsidiary of Bausch Health Companies Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas J. Appio | Interim CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 63","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $392K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Bausch + Lomb Corporation is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.1B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $66M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 87% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Bausch + Lomb (BLCO) Stock Could Be Cheap After Its 28% Gain","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-blco/bausch-lomb/news/bausch-lomb-blco-stock-could-be-cheap-after-its-28-gain","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793968608.472,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Are You Looking for a Top Momentum Pick? Why Bausch + Lomb (BLCO) is a Great Choice","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024635/are-you-looking-for-a-top-momentum-pick-why-bausch-lomb-blco-is-a-great-choice?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_10-3024635","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793894403.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Bausch + Lomb (BLCO) Might be Well Poised 